      "prompt": "You analyze passive underwater acoustic displays. Acoustic Hz and envelope modulation Hz are different quantities. A DEMON peak is not evidence of blade count, RPM, a ship class, or a unique physical source. Interference can create envelope beating. Treat received levels as uncalibrated digital amplitude. Keep overlapping components and uncertain associations. Filenames and hidden labels are unavailable. Do not invent evidence, measurements, probabilities, or physical identities. Report directly measured observable morphology even when its source is unknown; uncertain source identity alone is not a reason to withhold a measured observation. Return one JSON object only, without markdown. Use only requested schema keys. Use at most three frequency_track points per component and do not copy the full measurement table into the report.\nReturn {\"components\":[{\"id\":\"C1\",\"type\":\"tone|chirp|transient|broadband|modulation\",\"frequency_domain\":\"acoustic|modulation\",\"time_s\":[start,end],\"frequency_hz\":[low,high],\"frequency_track\":[[start,frequency_at_start],[end,frequency_at_end]],\"carrier_band_hz\":null,\"source_identity\":\"unknown\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"E1\"]}],\"relations\":[{\"type\":\"overlaps_time|harmonic_candidate|unresolved_association\",\"component_ids\":[\"C1\",\"C2\"],\"evidence_ids\":[\"E1\"]}],\"claims\":[{\"text\":\"a concise observable finding\",\"component_ids\":[\"C1\"],\"evidence_ids\":[\"E1\"],\"kind\":\"observation\"}],\"unresolved_questions\":[\"Which source produced these components?\"],\"abstained\":false}. Use at most 6 components and 3 brief claims. For chirps always supply at least two ordered frequency_track points, retaining rising versus falling direction. Evidence IDs must actually appear in the supplied measurement record; for image-only reports use empty evidence_ids. Intervals use the displayed original-recording seconds. Carrier bands are mandatory for modulation. Do not equate a component count with a phy